## 6. Selection mode

Chosen "Select games" → the shelf enters selection mode. Same page, same cards, same
filters, same search. A `selectionMode` flag on `state` plus a `selectedIds` Set.

**A reference mockup with approved styling accompanies this spec.** Match its
behaviour; adapt the CSS to the real card markup.

### Card behaviour

| Mode | Card tap | Info icon |
|---|---|---|
| Normal | opens detail modal | not rendered |
| Selection | toggles selection | opens detail modal |

### Visual treatment

- **Selection ring:** a dedicated overlay element above the cover art, `position:absolute; inset:0; z-index:3; border:2px solid; border-radius:10px; pointer-events:none`, transparent by default, `--bgs-gold` when selected.

  **Do not use CSS `outline` for this.** Outlines paint beneath child content, so the
  cover image covers them. This was tested and rejected.

- **Checkbox:** 22×22, top-left of the art, `z-index:4`. Dark translucent with an
  ivory border when unselected; `--bgs-gold` fill with a dark tick when selected.

- **Info icon:** 22×22 visible circle inside a **40×40 touch target**, top-right of
  the art, `z-index:4`.

- **Unselected cards:** art at `opacity:.62`, so selection reads at a glance across a
  6-column grid.

- The label plate is untouched in both modes.

### Filtering while selecting

Filters and search stay fully live. **Selections persist across filter changes** — a
game selected then filtered out stays selected, and the count keeps including it.
Losing selections because someone adjusted a filter would be infuriating.

The consequence is that the count can exceed the number of selected cards visible on
screen. The tray (§6.1) is what makes that legible rather than confusing, so the two
behaviours ship together — do not implement persistence without the tray.

### Bottom bar

Fixed to the viewport, appears on entering selection mode:

- **Cancel** on the left — exits selection mode, clears selections, closes the tray.
- **Count centred on the bar itself**, not in the space between the two buttons.
  Absolutely positioned at `left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%)`. With unequal button
  widths, `flex:1` does not centre it.
  - Primary line: "3 selected" followed by a chevron, same 13px size and same
    `--bgs-ivory` colour as the text, so the two read as one unit.
  - Sub-line: "Pick at least 1 more" counting down, then "Ready to go"
  - The whole count is a **button** (§6.1). Disabled at zero selections — nothing to
    show, so no false affordance.
- **Continue** on the right — disabled below 4 selections. No maximum.

Use `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` in the bottom padding so it clears the iPhone home
indicator.

### 6.1 Selected-games tray

Tapping the count expands a tray above the bottom bar listing everything currently
selected. Tapping again collapses it; so does tapping the scrim behind it.

This exists because selections persist across filter changes, which means the count
can exceed what's on screen. Without the tray, the host would have to clear filters
and hunt for a game to deselect it.

- **Slides up from the bottom**, rounded top corners, `max-height:52vh` with the list
  scrolling inside. Some shelf stays visible behind so the host doesn't lose their place.
- **Bottom padding must clear the bar** — the bar sits at a higher `z-index` and stays
  visible and usable while the tray is open.
- **Chevron rotates 180°** on open.
- **Each row:** cover thumbnail, title, a players/time line, and a remove button
  (34×34 touch target minimum).
- **Rows are in selection order**, not alphabetical — it reads as a running list of
  decisions.
- **"hidden by filters" tag** in `--bgs-gold-dim` on any row not in the current filtered
  set. This is what makes persistence safe: the host can see at a glance that picks are
  stashed outside the current view, rather than wondering why the count says 6 when
  only 4 cards are visible.
- **"Clear all"** in the tray header.
- **Auto-close when the last game is removed.** An empty tray is just an obstruction.
- Removing from the tray updates the grid immediately — the card's ring and checkbox
  clear if it's currently visible.

A reference implementation of all of this is in the accompanying mockup.

### Detail modal in selection mode

The existing detail card gains a **sticky action row** pinned to the bottom of the
modal while its content scrolls:

- Not selected → filled gold **"Add to tonight"**
- Selected → outlined gold **"In tonight's deck"** (tapping removes it)
- **Close** alongside it

**The modal does not auto-close on add.** The host may want to flip to the box back
after adding. In normal browsing the row shows only Close, so nothing changes about
today's experience.

